# Line endings are part of this project's correctness, not a style preference.
#
# Every chronicle line carries a roll, and the whole product rests on anyone
# being able to recompute it from the contract's own source. `npm run match`
# asks the chain for the bytes it is running and compares them to
# contracts/questline.py. With git left to its
# own devices that comparison is platform dependent: core.autocrlf rewrites the
# file to CRLF on a Windows checkout and LF everywhere else, so the same commit
# produces two different files and a check meant to prove "the deployed bytes are
# the source" fails for half the people who run it.
#
# Everything is therefore stored and checked out with LF, on every machine.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and must never be touched.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
